    {
        "name": "Ovarian Cysts",
        "name_ja": "卵巣嚢腫",
        "symptoms": {"bilateral_hair_loss", "bloated_abdomen", "crusty_nipples", "hormonal_behavior", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Ovarian cysts in guinea pigs are fluid-filled sacs that develop in the ovaries, extremely common in intact females >2 years old (30-70% of unspayed guinea pigs by age 3). Cysts result from persistent follicle stimulation or luteal cyst formation; estrogen secretion from cyst-bearing ovaries causes prolonged estrus, pseudopregnancy, or alopecia (symmetrical hair loss). CRITICAL: risk of cyst rupture with internal bleeding (acute emergency), secondary neoplasia (malignant transformation 5-10%), or infection/abscess formation. Diagnosis via ultrasound is definitive; surgical treatment (OVE/OVH) is curative.",
        "description_ja": "モルモットの卵巣嚢胞は液体で満たされた嚢胞で、未避妊雌（>2歳）に極度に多い（避妘なし雌の30-70%が3歳までに）。ホルモン様分泌による延長発情・偽妊娠・脱毛が発生。重大：破裂で内出血（急性緊急事態）、二次腫瘍化（5-10%）、感染/膿瘍のリスク。超音波で確定診断；手術（OVE/OVH）で根治。",
        "urgency": "moderate",
        "recommended_tests": ["ultrasound", "abdominal_x_ray", "hormonal_panel", "complete_blood_count"],
        "causes": "Persistent gonadotropin stimulation of ovarian follicles (FSH-producing cysts), impaired ovulation (anovulation cycles), or persistent corpus luteum formation (luteal cysts). Risk factors: intact status (no ovariohysterectomy), age >2 years (cumulative estrogen exposure), genetic predisposition (familial ovarian cysts), dietary factors (inadequate vitamin E/selenium increases oxidative stress), stress (alters GnRH pulsatility), previous dystocia (endometrial damage increases secondary cyst formation from uterine-ovarian inflammatory signaling).",
        "causes_ja": "持続的ゴナドトロピン刺激（FSH産生嚢胞）、排卵障害、または持続黄体形成。危険因子：避妘なし、>2歳年齢、遺伝的素因、栄養（ビタミンE/セレン不足）、ストレス、難産既往。",
        "pathophysiology": "Ovarian cysts develop from follicles that fail to ovulate, accumulating follicular fluid under continued hormonal stimulation. Granulosa cells within cyst wall secrete estrogen (even without ovulation), causing prolonged estral cycle and systemic estrogenic signs. Cyst rupture causes acute hemorrhage into peritoneal cavity, triggering peritoneal irritation/inflammation. Secondary transformation to cystic neoplasia (adenocarcinoma, granulosa cell tumor) occurs in 5-10% of cases, particularly with chronic cyst persistence >6-12 months. Chronic estrogen exposure predisposes to endometrial hyperplasia, uterine cysts, and eventual pyometra risk (even in non-breeding animals). Cyst torsion (rotation of ovarian pedicle) causes acute vascular compromise and ovarian infarction, presenting as acute abdomen.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "卵巣嚢胞は排卵不全の濾胞から発生、継続ホルモン刺激で液体蓄積。嚢胞壁の顆粒膜細胞がエストロゲン分泌（無排卵でも）、延長発情周期と全身エストロゲン徴候。嚢胞破裂で腹腔急性出血、腹膜刺激。6-12ヶ月の慢性嚢胞で5-10%が腺癌/顆粒膜細胞腫に転化。慢性エストロゲン曝露で子宮内膜過形成・子宮嚢胞・子宮蓄膿症リスク。嚢胞捻転で血管圧迫と卵巣梗塞。",
        "treatment": "TREATMENT OPTIONS (choose based on cyst characteristics, age, breeding status): 1) MEDICAL MANAGEMENT (for functional cysts with minimal symptoms; trial 4-8 weeks): a) GnRH AGONIST: Deslorelin implant 4.7 mg SC (induces desensitization of pituitary, suppresses FSH; lasts 3-6 months per implant). Monitor ultrasound at weeks 4-6 (cyst size should decrease 30-50% if FSH-responsive). Alternative: leuprolide acetate 75-100 μg/kg SC q4 weeks × 8 weeks (similar mechanism, less convenient). b) hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin): 1,000 IU/kg IM every 7 days × 2-3 doses (triggers ovulation in functional cysts; ONLY effective if cyst is FSH-responsive, not for persistent corpus luteum). Monitor for ovulation (cessation of estrus, behavioral change). c) MONITORING: weekly ultrasound × 4 weeks, then monthly (assess cyst size, complications). If cyst persists >4-8 weeks despite medical management → surgical removal indicated. 2) PERCUTANEOUS NEEDLE ASPIRATION (temporary relief only; recurrence rate 80%+ within weeks): ultrasound-guided fine-needle aspiration under brief isoflurane sedation (cyst contents vacuumed out, partial collapse of cyst wall). Appropriate ONLY as temporary bridge to surgery in critical patients. 3) SURGICAL MANAGEMENT (OVE/OVH—DEFINITIVE TREATMENT; recommended for cysts >20 mm, multiple cysts, symptoms refractory to medical management, or cyst rupture): a) PRE-OPERATIVE ASSESSMENT: ultrasound to assess cyst characteristics (simple fluid-filled vs complex/hemorrhagic), size, number, evidence of rupture (free peritoneal fluid), presence of concurrent uterine pathology (pyometra, hyperplasia). Blood chemistry for anesthetic risk. b) ANESTHESIA PROTOCOL (non-narcotic, minimize GI suppression): pre-medication dexmedetomidine 5-10 μg/kg IM, mask induction isoflurane (vaporizer 3-4%), maintain 1.5-2.5% isoflurane in oxygen. Warm IV fluids (37°C) during surgery. c) SURGICAL TECHNIQUE: ventral midline laparotomy (25-35 mm incision), exteriorize ovary carefully (avoid cyst rupture—use gentle handling), ligate ovarian and uterine vessels with 4-0 silk or absorbable suture. Option 1: Partial OVE (remove affected ovary only, preserve contralateral ovary if unaffected and breeding possible). Option 2: Full OVE/OVH (remove both ovaries and uterus—recommended for non-breeding animals due to >50% risk of contralateral cyst development within 12-24 months). Close linea alba with 4-0 absorbable suture, skin with tissue adhesive. d) IF CYST RUPTURE ENCOUNTERED: assess for hemorrhage, irrigate peritoneal cavity gently with warm 0.9% saline, remove clots/blood, ensure hemostasis of ovarian vessel. Bleeding >5 mL into peritoneum indicates vessel injury—ligate or cauterize. Watch for ongoing bleeding post-op (abdominal distension >24h post-op = hemorrhage suspect, may need re-operation). 4) POST-OPERATIVE CARE (CRITICAL for survival): a) VITAMIN C SUPPLEMENTATION—MANDATORY: ascorbic acid 50-100 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 10-14 days post-op (guinea pigs cannot synthesize C; surgery depletes reserves). b) ANALGESIA: meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7 days (NOT buprenorphine—opioids suppress GI motility). c) ANTIBIOTICS: enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 14 days (covers gram-negatives from peritoneal translocation if rupture occurred). d) IV/SC FLUIDS: LRS 10-20 mL/kg/day × 48-72 hours (hemorrhage may have occurred if rupture encountered). e) GI SUPPORT CRITICAL: timothy hay ad libitum (NO restriction—cecal function requires continuous fiber), high-quality pellets, probiotics (FortiFlora 1-2 sachets q12h × 7-10 days). f) TEMPERATURE CONTROL: maintain 22-24°C (optimal recovery). g) MONITORING: daily temperature, appetite, fecal output (should resume 12-24h post-op). Abdominal distension >24h = hemorrhage suspect. Pain assessment (should improve by post-op day 2-3; persistence = complication). 5) EMERGENCY COMPLICATIONS: Cyst rupture with uncontrolled hemorrhage: transfuse if possible (matched guinea pig blood 10-15 mL/kg if available), continue IV fluids, monitor for shock (pale mucous membranes, weak pulses, hypothermia). Peritonitis from infection/rupture: aggressive fluids, maximize antibiotics (add metronidazole 20 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days), consider re-operation if refractory to antibiotics.",
        "treatment_ja": "治療選択肢（嚢胞特性、年齢、育種状態で選択）：1) 医学的管理（機能性嚢胞で最小症状；4-8週試行）：a) GnRH アゴニスト：デスロレリンインプラント 4.7 mg SC（下垂体脱感作で FSH 抑制；3-6ヶ月/インプラント）。4-6週で超音波監視（嚢胞30-50%縮小予期）。代替：ロイプロリド酢酸 75-100 μg/kg SC q4週 × 8週。b) hCG：1,000 IU/kg IM q7日 × 2-3回（機能性嚢胞排卵誘発）。発情停止監視。c) 監視：週1回超音波 × 4週、その後月1回。4-8週で嚢胞遷延 → 手術適応。2) 経皮針吸引（一時的；再発率 80%+）。3) 外科管理（OVE/OVH—根治的）：a) 術前評価：超音波で嚢胞特性評価、破裂証拠、子宮病理。b) 麻酔：デクスメデトミジン 5-10 μg/kg IM + イソフルラン。c) 手術：腹部正中小開腸、卵巣を注意深く外側化、血管結紮。選択肢1：部分 OVE（患側卵巣のみ除去）。選択肢2：全 OVE/OVH（推奨—>50%対側嚢胞発生リスク 12-24ヶ月）。d) 破裂時：灌流、止血確認、出血継続監視。4) 術後管理（生存に重大）：a) ビタミンC補充必須：アスコルビン酸 50-100 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 10-14日。b) 鎮痛：メロキシカム 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7日。c) 抗菌薬：エンロフロキサシン 5-10 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 14日。d) IV/SC輸液：LRS 10-20 mL/kg/日 × 48-72時間。e) GI支持：ティモシーヘイ給与量制限なし、プロバイオティクス。f) 温度：22-24°C。g) 監視：温度、食欲、排便。5) 緊急合併症：破裂出血：輸血考慮、IV輸液、ショック監視。腹膜炎：積極的輸液、抗菌薬最大化。",
        "prevention": "CRITICAL PREVENTION (ovarian cysts are largely preventable via spaying): 1) SPAYING—MOST EFFECTIVE PREVENTION: Ovariohysterectomy before age 2 years virtually eliminates ovarian cyst risk (100% prevention if performed before cyst development). Recommend OVE/OVH in all non-breeding females by 12-18 months of age. Early spaying also prevents secondary endometrial disease (hyperplasia, pyometra—40-50% incidence by age 4-5 in unspayed animals). 2) BREEDING MANAGEMENT (for breeding females): Select for genetic resistance (avoid breeding females with cyst history or whose mothers had cysts). Limit breeding to females 2-4 years old (avoid <12 months—immature; avoid >4 years—increased cyst risk). Mandatory yearly ultrasound screening starting age 1.5 years (detect small cysts before symptoms). Breeding females with cysts should be retired after current litter and spayed. 3) NUTRITION (supportive but not curative): Vitamin E 20-50 IU/kg/day (antioxidant support), selenium 0.3-0.5 μg/kg/day (cofactor for antioxidant enzymes), maintain adequate vitamin A (prevent luteal phase insufficiency), calcium 1.2-1.5% (supports hormone metabolism). High-quality timothy hay ad libitum, balanced pellets 15-20g/day, fresh vegetables (vitamin C source). 4) STRESS REDUCTION: minimize environmental stressors (loud noise, overcrowding, cage mates conflict), maintain stable 22-24°C temperature, consistent 12h light/dark cycle (disruption increases GnRH pulsatility abnormalities). 5) MONITORING (for breeding females retained): quarterly ultrasound starting age 2 years (assess ovarian volume, cyst number/size). If ultrasound shows cyst >10 mm, discuss management options (medical vs surgical). If ultrasound shows multiple cysts or rapid growth (>5 mm/month), recommend OVE. 6) POST-DYSTOCIA CARE: females with dystocia history have increased secondary cyst formation due to endometrial inflammation—consider OVE post-treatment rather than re-breeding.",
        "prevention_ja": "重大予防（卵巣嚢胞は避妘で大部分予防可能）：1) 避妘—最も効果的予防：OVE/OVH を2歳前に実施で嚢胞リスク100%除去。12-18ヶ月齢までに全非育種雌に推奨。早期避妘で子宮内膜疾患（4-5歳で40-50%発生）も予防。2) 育種管理（育種雌）：遺伝的抵抗性選別（嚢胞既往雌の育種禁止）。2-4歳の育種のみ（<12ヶ月回避—未成熟；>4歳回避—高リスク）。1.5歳から年1回超音波（嚢胞症状前検出）。育種中嚢胞雌は現産仔後に退役・避妘。3) 栄養：ビタミンE 20-50 IU/kg/日、セレン 0.3-0.5 μg/kg/日、ビタミンA、カルシウム 1.2-1.5%。4) ストレス軽減：環境ストレス最小化、温度 22-24°C、12h明暗周期。5) 監視（保持育種雌）：2歳から四半期超音波（卵巣体積、嚢胞数/サイズ）。>10 mm 嚢胞 → 管理選択肢相談。複数嚢胞または急速成長（>5 mm/月）→ OVE 推奨。6) 難産後ケア：難産既往雌は子宮内膜炎から二次嚢胞形成増加—再育種より OVE 推奨。",
        "prognosis": "EXCELLENT with early surgical intervention: OVE/OVH cure rate >98% (cysts do not recur after ovary removal). Medical management success (GnRH agonist trial) 50-70% for FSH-responsive functional cysts; however, >50% recur within 6-12 months if ovaries retained. Without intervention, prognosis depends on cyst type: simple follicular cysts may persist asymptomatically for years (no treatment needed if <20 mm and non-symptomatic), but 10-15% rupture spontaneously causing acute hemorrhage (mortality 30-40% even with emergency treatment). Functional cysts show variable course—some regress spontaneously (20-30%), while others progress to large, hormone-secreting cysts requiring surgery. Long-term: unspayed females with cysts have >50% risk of developing concurrent uterine disease (pyometra, hyperplasia) within 12-24 months even if ovarian cysts managed medically. Risk of malignant transformation: 5-10% of persistent cysts >12 months develop into adenocarcinoma or granulosa cell tumor (mortality near 100% if diagnosed—metastatic spread common by diagnosis time). Post-surgical prognosis: females surviving OVE/OVH have normal lifespan; no impact on longevity. Quality of life dramatically improves post-surgery (hair regrowth within 4-6 weeks, behavioral normalization within 1-2 weeks).",
        "prognosis_ja": "早期手術介入で優秀：OVE/OVH 治癒率 >98%。医学的管理成功（GnRH アゴニスト試行）FSH反応性嚢胞で 50-70%；但し卵巣保持で >50% が 6-12ヶ月以内に再発。無治療で進過は嚢胞型に依存：単純濾胞嚢胞は無症状で数年遷延（<20 mm でアトピーなら治療不要），但し 10-15% が自発破裂（急性出血で死亡率 30-40%）。機能性嚢胞は可変進過—20-30% が自然消退、他は大型ホルモン分泌嚢胞で手術要。長期：未避妘嚢胞雌で >50% が 12-24ヶ月で並存子宮疾患（子宮蓄膿症、過形成）発生。悪性転化リスク：5-10% で腺癌/顆粒膜細胞腫に（診断時転移は普通で死亡率 ~100%）。術後：生存雌は正常寿命；生活の質が劇的改善（毛髪再生 4-6週、行動正常化 1-2週）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute", "chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Dystocia",
        "name_ja": "難産",
        "symptoms": {"straining", "lethargy", "vaginal_bleeding", "distress_vocalizations", "no_delivery"},
        "description": "Dystocia in guinea pigs is a critical obstetric emergency, especially in first-time breeders over 6-8 months old when pelvic fusion is complete.",
        "description_ja": "分娩困難で、8か月齢以降に初めて交配した場合は特に危険です。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["abdominal_x_ray", "ultrasound", "physical_exam"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Age-related pelvic fusion: guinea pig pelvis begins fusing at 6-8 months; first breeding after 8 months carries 10-50% dystocia risk (20% mortality); 2) Fetal size mismatch: large fetuses (especially from males with larger body mass), long inter-breeding intervals select for larger fetuses; 3) Maternal factors: obesity (pelvic canal narrowing), uterine inertia (inadequate calcium/magnesium), poor condition, stress; 4) Fetal presentation: breech/transverse presentation, fetal deformity (anasarca, hydrocephalus).",
        "causes_ja": "モルモットの難産の原因：年齢関連骨盤融合（モルモット骨盤は6-8ヶ月で融合開始；初産>8ヶ月で難産リスク10-50%、死亡率20%）。胎児サイズ不均合（雄から大型胎児、長い育種間隔で大型選抜）。母体因子（肥満で骨盤狭窄、子宮無力でカルシウム/マグネシウム欠乏、不良体況、ストレス）。胎児プレゼンテーション（骨盤位/横位、奇形）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Dystocia in guinea pigs occurs when the fetuses cannot pass through the pelvic canal due to pelvic fusion, fetal size, or maternal factors. In guinea pigs (unlike mice/rats), the fetuses are large relative to body size, and pelvic fusion after ~6-8 months makes passage impossible. Labor begins with strong uterine contractions (myometrial oxytocin-driven), but if obstruction persists >4-6 hours, uterine ischemia develops. Prolonged labor (>12 hours) causes maternal metabolic acidosis, fetal hypoxia, uterine rupture. Guinea pig fetuses have long gestation (63-70 days); delayed delivery →fetal death, maceration, absorption. Maternal sepsis/peritonitis develops if uterus ruptures or fetus dies in utero.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "モルモットの難産は骨盤融合、胎児サイズ、または母体因子で胎児が骨盤管を通過できない病態。モルモット（ネズミと異なり）は胎児が体サイズに対して大きく、~6-8ヶ月後の骨盤融合で通過不可能。分娩は強い子宮収縮（筋層オキシトシン駆動）で始まるが、閉塞が>4-6時間続くと子宮虚血発生。長期分娩（>12時間）で母体代謝性アシドーシス、胎児低酸素血症、子宮破裂。モルモット胎児は長い妊娠期間（63-70日）；遅延分娩→胎児死亡、腐敗、吸収。子宮破裂または子宮内胎児死亡で母体敗血症/腹膜炎。",
        "treatment": "CRITICAL: Guinea pig dystocia is largely non-responsive to medical management due to structural pelvic obstruction. 1) Stabilization: IV fluids (lactated Ringer's 50-100 mL/kg), pain management (meloxicam 0.2-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h), oxygen if respiratory distress, vitamin C 50-100 mg/kg SC (guinea pigs cannot synthesize vitamin C; stress depletes stores). 2) Initial medical attempt (brief, <30 min if obstruction suspected): Calcium gluconate 50-100 mg/kg SC (rare cases respond), oxytocin 0.5-3 IU/kg SC/IM single dose (success <20% in guinea pigs due to anatomical obstruction). 3) EMERGENCY CESAREAN SECTION (definitive treatment): Anesthesia—isoflurane (avoid injectable anesthetics; guinea pigs very sensitive, apneic with injectable drugs). Approach: low midline incision, exteriorize uterus, incise at antimesentric border, remove all fetuses carefully. Uterotomy closure: 4-0 or 5-0 absorbable suture in simple interrupted pattern. Abdominal wall: 4-0 absorbable. Skin: 4-0 non-absorbable or tissue adhesive. 4) Post-operative: Analgesia critical—meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7 days (short duration due to GI ulcer risk), antibiotics if infection risk (enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg SC/IM q12h × 10-14 days), IV fluids 24-48h, vitamin C 50-100 mg/kg SC q12h, warm environment (18-24°C), allow nursing if pups viable.",
        "treatment_ja": "モルモットの難産治療：重要：構造的骨盤閉塞のため医学的管理に大部分非反応性。1) 安定化：輸液（乳酸リンガー50-100 mL/kg）、鎮痛（メロキシカム0.2-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h）、呼吸窮迫時酸素、ビタミンC補給（モルモットはビタミンC合成不可；ストレスで枯渇）。2) 初期医学的試み（<30分、閉塞疑われる場合短縮）：グルコン酸カルシウム50-100 mg/kg SC（稀に反応）、オキシトシン0.5-3 IU/kg SC/IM 1回（モルモットでは解剖学的閉塞で成功<20%）。3) 緊急帝王切開（決定的治療）：イソフルラン麻酔（注射薬回避；モルモール麻酔感受性高い）。低腹部正中切開、子宮外転、反中間膜部切開、胎児慎重除去。子宮縫合：4-0または5-0吸収性簡単割符。腹壁：4-0吸収性。皮膚：4-0非吸収性または接着剤。4) 術後：鎮痛重要—メロキシカム0.3-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7日、抗菌薬（エンロフロキサシン5-10 mg/kg SC/IM q12h × 10-14日）、輸液24-48h、ビタミンC 50-100 mg/kg SC q12h、温度管理（18-24℃）、産仔生存時授乳許可。",
        "prevention": "CRITICAL PREVENTION: 1) Breed females ONLY before 5-6 months of age (before pelvic fusion). Late first breeding (>8 months) carries 20% maternal mortality; breeding should be completed by 6 months maximum. 2) Selective breeding: avoid breeding large individuals to each other; large males + large females = large fetuses + high dystocia risk. 3) Nutrition: adequate calcium (1,000-1,500 mg/kg diet), magnesium (300-400 mg/kg), vitamin C (50 mg/kg minimum), maintain ideal body weight (avoid obesity). 4) Monitoring: ultrasound at day 30-40 gestation to confirm viability, assess litter size (larger litters = larger individual fetuses potentially). 5) Limit breeding: do not breed same female consecutively; allow 6-week rest between litters. 6) Spay if first breeding delayed beyond 5-6 months (dystocia risk too high for benefit).",
        "prevention_ja": "モルモットの難産予防：重要：1) 5-6ヶ月齢前のみ繁殖（骨盤融合前）。初産>8ヶ月で母体死亡率20%；繁殖は最大6ヶ月までに完了。2) 選択育種：大型個体同士の繁殖回避；大雄+大雌=大型胎児で難産リスク。3) 栄養：十分なカルシウム（1,000-1,500 mg/kg食）、マグネシウム（300-400 mg/kg）、ビタミンC（最小50 mg/kg）、理想体重維持。4) 監視：妊娠30-40日で超音波確認、産仔数評価（大産仔数=潜在的に大型個体）。5) 繁殖制限：同じメス連続繁殖回避；産仔間6週間休止。6) 初産が5-6ヶ月齢超過なら避妊（難産リスク利益を上回る）。",
        "prognosis": "Guarded to poor if medical management attempted. With prompt cesarean section (within 1-2 hours of dystocia onset), maternal survival 60-75%; delayed surgery (>4-6 hours): mortality >80%. Fetus survival decreases significantly with prolonged dystocia; >12 hours →fetal demise in most cases. Post-cesarean recovery good (6-8 week recouvery) if no sepsis develops. CRITICAL: Late breeding (>8 months) carries inherently poor prognosis due to pelvic anatomy. Best strategy is prevention via early breeding (before 6 months) or spaying if breeding delayed.",
        "prognosis_ja": "モルモット難産の予後：医学的管理試みなら慎重〜不良。迅速帝王切開（発症から1-2時間以内）で母体生存率60-75%；遅延手術（>4-6時間）で死亡率>80%。胎児生存は長期難産で著減；>12時間で大部分胎児死亡。術後回復は敗血症なしで良好（6-8週回復）。重要：初産>8ヶ月は骨盤解剖学的に予後本来的に不良。最良の戦略は早期繁殖（6ヶ月前）による予防または繁殖延期時の避妊。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Pregnancy Toxemia (Ketosis)",
        "name_ja": "妊娠中毒症（ケトーシス）",
        "symptoms": {"appetite_loss", "lethargy", "labored_breathing", "seizures", "muscle_spasms", "sudden_death_risk"},
        "description": "Pregnancy Toxemia (Ketosis) in guinea pigs is a life-threatening metabolic emergency in late pregnancy (day 50+) or early lactation, with mortality 50-100% if untreated.",
        "description_ja": "妊娠後期または産後早期の代謝性危機で、しばしば致命的です。肥満の雌で最もリスクが高くなります。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["blood_work", "urinalysis", "blood_glucose", "blood_ketones", "liver_function"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Metabolic: negative energy balance in late pregnancy (fetuses rapidly grow, demanding 70%+ of maternal glucose), hepatic lipid mobilization → ketone body accumulation (beta-hydroxybutyrate, acetoacetate, acetone); 2) Risk factors: obesity (pre-breeding weight >1,500g), large litter size (>3 fetuses), multiparity (repeated pregnancies), malnutrition (especially vitamin C/B deficiency), stress; 3) Pathophysiology: guinea pigs cannot synthesize glucose from protein effectively; during pregnancy, fetal demand exceeds hepatic gluconeogenesis capacity, forcing ketone metabolism → metabolic acidosis.",
        "causes_ja": "モルモットの妊娠中毒症（ケトーシス）の原因：代謝性：妊娠後期での負のエネルギーバランス（胎児が急速成長、母体グルコースの70%以上要求）、肝臓脂質動員→ケトン体蓄積。リスク因子：肥満（育種前体重>1,500g）、大産仔数（>3胎児）、多産性、栄養不良（特にビタミンC/B欠乏）、ストレス。モルモットはタンパク質からグルコース合成不能；妊娠中は胎児要求が肝糖新生容量を超える→ケトン代謝→代謝性アシドーシス。",
        "pathophysiology": "Pregnancy toxemia develops when maternal hepatic glucose production cannot meet fetal demands during late pregnancy. Guinea pigs have limited capacity for gluconeogenesis from amino acids (unlike other rodents). As pregnancy progresses (day 50-70), fetal mass increases exponentially; glucose uptake by fetuses + mammary tissue exceeds hepatic production. Liver mobilizes fatty acids for energy, producing excess ketone bodies (beta-hydroxybutyrate >>acetoacetate). Severe ketosis (blood ketones >5 mmol/L) causes metabolic acidosis, electrolyte imbalance, cerebral edema. Seizures result from hypokalemia + acidosis + cerebral edema. Hypoglycemia (<3 mmol/L = 54 mg/dL) triggers loss of consciousness. Without intervention, respiratory failure, coma, death within 24-48 hours.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "妊娠中毒症は母体肝糖生産が妊娠後期の胎児要求に満たない病態で生じる。モルモットはアミノ酸からの糖新生能力制限（他げっ歯類と異なり）。妊娠が進む（50-70日）と胎児質量が指数関数的増加；胎児+乳腺のグルコース取得が肝生産を超える。肝臓は脂肪酸をエネルギーに動員、過剰ケトン体産生。重度ケトーシス（血中ケトン>5 mmol/L）で代謝性アシドーシス、電解質不均衡、脳浮腫。けいれんはカリウム低下+アシドーシス+脳浮腫で生じる。低血糖（<3 mmol/L=54 mg/dL）で意識喪失。無治療で呼吸不全→昏睡→24-48時間で死亡。",
        "treatment": "CRITICAL EMERGENCY—immediate intervention required: 1) Blood work STAT: blood glucose, ketones (urine ketones positive), blood gas (pH <7.35 acidemia), electrolytes (hypokalemia common). 2) Rapid IV glucose: 5% dextrose 50-100 mL IV over 5-10 min (bolus), then 5% dextrose 50-100 mL/kg/day IV in LRS for 24-48h. If IV access difficult: 50% dextrose 0.5-1 mL SC q4-6h as emergency bridge. 3) Aggressive nutritional support: syringe feeding q3-4h with high-energy food (infant formula 1:1 with water, hay-based paste with molasses, fruit puree) for 5-7 days. Goal: 100 kcal/kg/day minimum. 4) Supportive fluids: LRS 50-100 mL/kg/day IV/SC for 48-72h to correct acidosis + electrolyte derangement. 5) Vitamin C 100 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 5-7 days (guinea pigs cannot synthesize vitamin C; stress depletes stores; deficiency perpetuates metabolic crisis). 6) Pain/stress management: meloxicam 0.2-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h × 5 days (minimize stress-induced gluconeogenesis inhibition). 7) EMERGENCY CESAREAN SECTION & NON-NARCOTIC ANESTHESIA: IF near term (day 60+) AND deteriorating rapidly (seizures, coma, respiratory distress, persistent hypoglycemia despite glucose support), emergency cesarean may be LIFESAVING. **CRITICAL PRE-OPERATIVE GLUCOSE MANAGEMENT**: ensure blood glucose 100-150 mg/dL before induction; continue 5% dextrose IV during entire procedure. **NON-NARCOTIC ANESTHESIA PROTOCOL FOR METABOLICALLY COMPROMISED GUINEA PIG**: (a) Pre-anesthetic: Dexmedetomidine 10 μg/kg IM (or medetomidine 10 μg/kg if DEX unavailable; alpha-2 agents acceptable in emergency cesarean as they preserve glucose homeostasis better than opioids) with butorphanol 0.4 mg/kg IM (fentanyl/morphine avoided—respiratory depression worsens hypercapnia/acidosis). (b) Induction: Alfaxalone 5-7 mg/kg IV slow OR isoflurane induction by mask (mask induction PREFERRED in acidotic/hypoglycemic animals to avoid IV complications). AVOID propofol (causes severe hypoglycemia) and ketamine (dangerous with severe acidosis). (c) Maintenance: Isoflurane 1.5-2.5% in 100% O₂ with assisted IPPV (critical: maintain EtCO₂ 35-40 mmHg—avoid hypocapnia which worsens acidosis, avoid hypercapnia which adds respiratory acidosis). (d) LOCAL INFILTRATION ANALGESIA: Pre-operative bupivacaine 0.5% 2 mg/kg infiltrated around uterine vessels and planned incision line (reduces inhalational agent requirement, preserves MAP in hemodynamically vulnerable animal). (e) FETAL MONITORING: Maintain maternal SPO₂ >95% (100% O₂), MAP >50-60 mmHg (use warm IV fluids, heating pad), core body temp 36-37°C (hypothermia exacerbates metabolic crisis). If Doppler ultrasound available, monitor fetal heart rate. (f) EMERGENCY EQUIPMENT: Have atipamezole available (alpha-2 reversal), dextrose 50% IV boluses for perioperative hypoglycemia, emergency defibrillator. 8) Monitor continuously: blood glucose q4h target 80-120 mg/dL, blood gas q12h, electrolytes q12h, urine ketones. Post-cesarean: aggressive medical management continues (IV glucose, fluids, vitamin C) for 48-72h minimum.",
        "treatment_ja": "モルモットの妊娠中毒症：重大な緊急事態—迅速介入必須：1) 血液検査STAT：血糖、ケトン体（尿ケトン陽性）、血液ガス（pH <7.35 acidemia）、電解質（低カリウム多い）。2) 迅速IV グルコース：5%デキストロース50-100 mL IV × 5-10分（ボーラス）、次に5%デキストロース50-100 mL/kg/日 IV LRS 24-48h。IV困難時：50%デキストロース0.5-1 mL SC q4-6h緊急橋渡し。3) 積極的栄養補給：syringe給餌 q3-4時間高エネルギー食（ベビー粉ミルク1:1水、干し草ペーストmolasses、フルーツピューレ）× 5-7日。目標：100 kcal/kg/日最小。4) 支持流動食：LRS 50-100 mL/kg/日 IV/SC × 48-72h でアシドーシス+電解質異常是正。5) ビタミンC 100 mg/kg SC/PO q12h × 5-7日（モルモットはビタミンC合成不可；ストレスで枯渇；欠乏で代謝危機遷延）。6) 疼痛/ストレス管理：メロキシカム0.2-0.5 mg/kg SC q12h × 5日（ストレス誘発糖新生抑制最小化）。7) 緊急帝王切開と非麻薬性麻酔：妊娠60日以上かつ急速悪化（けいれん、昏睡、呼吸窮迫、ブドウ糖補給にもかかわらず持続低血糖）なら緊急帝王切開は生命救助可能。**重大な術前ブドウ糖管理**：導入前に血糖100-150 mg/dL確保；手術全体で5%デキストロース IV継続。**代謝的に代償不全のモルモット用非麻薬性麻酔プロトコル**：(a) 麻酔前：デクスメデトミジン10 μg/kg IM（またはMED 10 μg/kg；α2作動薬は緊急帝王切開で許容—オピオイドより糖恒常性保持が良好）+ ブトルファノール0.4 mg/kg IM（フェンタニル/モルヒネ避けて—呼吸抑制が高炭酸血症/アシドーシス悪化）。(b) 導入：アルファキサロン5-7 mg/kg IV 緩速またはイソフルラン吸入マスク導入（マスク導入が好適—酸性/低血糖動物では IV合併症リスク回避）。プロポフォール避ける（重度低血糖）、ケタミン避ける（重度アシドーシスで危険）。(c) 維持：イソフルラン1.5-2.5%を100% O₂で、IPPV補助（重大：EtCO₂ 35-40 mmHg維持—低炭酸血症で アシドーシス悪化回避、高炭酸血症で呼吸性アシドーシス追加回避）。(d) 局所浸潤鎮痛：術前ブピバカイン0.5% 2 mg/kg を子宮血管周囲・予定切開部位に浸潤（吸入麻酔要件軽減、血行動態脆弱動物でMAP保持）。(e) 胎児監視：母体SPO₂ >95%（100% O₂）、MAP >50-60 mmHg維持（温い IV液体、ヒーティングパッド使用）、中核体温36-37°C（低体温が代謝危機悪化）。ドップラー超音波で胎児心拍監視。(f) 緊急機材：アティパメゾール（α2拮抗薬）、デキストロース50% IV ボーラス周術期低血糖用、緊急除細動器。8) 継続監視：血糖 q4h 目標80-120 mg/dL、血液ガス q12h、電解質 q12h、尿ケトン。術後：積極的医学管理（IV グルコース、輸液、ビタミンC）を48-72時間最小限継続。",
        "prevention": "Prevention is CRITICAL (mortality/morbidity so high): 1) Avoid obesity: maintain pre-breeding weight <1,200-1,300g (ideally 900-1,100g), weigh females monthly during pregnancy; obesity during gestation increases ketosis risk 5-10×. 2) Breed only young guinea pigs (4-8 months old): older/multipara females at higher risk. 3) Limit litter size: do not breed large females to large males (select for smaller offspring); large litters (>4) increase metabolic demand. 4) Adequate nutrition during pregnancy: increase hay intake (timothy hay 70% diet), supplement with pellets (250g body weight = 200-300g pellets/day), provide vitamin C 50-100 mg/kg/day (critical deficiency perpetuates metabolic crisis). 5) Stress reduction: minimize handling during late pregnancy (day 50+); stress suppresses gluconeogenesis. 6) Avoid late breeding: do not breed females >8-10 months old (gestation + lactation combined with aging increases risk). 7) Consider spaying obese females or females with history of toxemia (recurrence risk 50%+ if attempt rebreeding). 8) Early detection: weigh female daily from day 40 onward; sudden weight loss >20g = warning sign; measure blood glucose if anorexia/lethargy appears.",
        "prevention_ja": "妊娠中毒症の予防は重大（死亡/罹患率高い）：1) 肥満回避：育種前体重<1,200-1,300g維持（理想900-1,100g）、妊娠中月1回体重測定；妊娠中肥満はケトーシスリスク5-10倍。2) 若いモルモットのみ繁殖（4-8ヶ月齢）：高齢/多産雌はリスク高。3) 産仔数制限：大雌を大雄に繁殖させない（小型産仔選抜）；大産仔数（>4）で代謝要求増加。4) 妊娠中栄養：チモシー干し草摂取増加（70%食）、ペレット補充（250g体重=200-300g ペレット/日）、ビタミンC 50-100 mg/kg/日提供（重大欠乏で代謝危機遷延）。5) ストレス軽減：妊娠後期（50日以上）での取扱い最小化；ストレスで糖新生抑制。6) 遅延繁殖回避：>8-10ヶ月齢雌を繁殖させない。7) 肥満雌または中毒症既往の避妊考慮（再発リスク50%以上）。8) 早期発見：40日から毎日体重測定；体重突然減少>20g=警告信号；食欲不振/沈鬱で血糖測定。",
        "prognosis": "CRITICAL: mortality 50-100% without treatment. With EARLY intervention (within 6-12 hours of symptom onset), survival 40-60%. Late intervention (>24-48 hours): mortality >90%. Deaths typically occur from metabolic acidosis, cerebral edema with seizures, or respiratory failure. Survivors may have permanent neurological sequelae if seizures were prolonged. If cesarean section needed: additional anesthetic risk; post-operative mortality increases to 60-80% even with surgery. Females that survive one episode of toxemia carry 50%+ risk of recurrence if rebreed; spaying recommended post-recovery.",
        "prognosis_ja": "妊娠中毒症の予後：重大：無治療で死亡率50-100%。早期介入（症状発症から6-12時間以内）で生存率40-60%。遅延介入（>24-48時間）で死亡率>90%。死亡は代謝性アシドーシス、けいれん伴う脳浮腫、または呼吸不全から。生存者は延長けいれんで永続的神経学的後遺症あり。帝王切開が必要なら：追加麻酔リスク；術後死亡率増加して60-80%。1回の中毒症から生存した雌は再繁殖時に再発リスク50%以上；回復後の避妊を推奨。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Pyometra",
        "name_ja": "子宮蓄膿症",
        "symptoms": {"vaginal_discharge", "bloated_abdomen", "lethargy", "appetite_loss", "excessive_thirst", "fever"},
        "description": "Pyometra is a life-threatening uterine bacterial infection requiring emergency ovariohysterectomy. Guinea pigs progress to sepsis/death within 48-96 hours without treatment.",
        "description_ja": "子宮内に膿が溜まる感染症で、緊急手術が必要です。モルモットは無治療で48-96時間で敗血症/死亡に進行。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["ultrasound", "blood_work", "abdominal_x_ray", "culture_sensitivity"],
        "causes": "Caused by bacterial colonization of the uterus during luteal phase (progesterone-induced endometrial receptivity). Staphylococcus aureus, Escherichia coli, Pasteurella multocida, and Streptococcus spp. most common. Routes: ascending infection from perineum, hematogenous spread, direct tissue inoculation from dystocia. Risk factors: intact females >12-18 months old (age >3 years = 10-fold risk increase), previous unsuccessful breeding attempts (chronic estrogen exposure), poor hygiene, immunosuppression, concurrent illness (malnutrition, vitamin C deficiency).",
        "causes_ja": "黄体ホルモン誘導子宮内膜受容性中の細菌コロニー化。黄色ブドウ球菌、大腸菌、多様性パスツレラ、連鎖球菌が最多。経路：会陰部上行感染、菌血症、難産からの直接組織接種。危険因子：>12-18ヶ月齢避妊されない雌（>3歳=10倍リスク増加）、無成功育種試行歴（慢性エストロゲン曝露）、不衛生、免疫抑制、併発疾患（栄養不良、ビタミンC欠乏）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Guinea pig pyometra develops as bacteria (especially gram-negative) colonize progesterone-prepared endometrium. Bacterial endotoxins (LPS) trigger acute inflammatory cascade: cytokine release (TNF-α, IL-6, IL-8), complement activation, prostaglandin surge. Neutrophil infiltration leads to abscess formation, tissue necrosis, suppurative exudate accumulation. Uterine distension increases systemic endotoxin absorption via impaired barrier function. Rapid progression to septic shock: fever→tachycardia (HR >250 bpm)→shock→DIC→multi-organ failure. Guinea pigs lack spleen-equivalent lymphoid tissue; cannot mount effective systemic immune response (unlike dogs/cats). Time to critical illness: <48 hours for closed-type, <72 hours for open-type. Without treatment: 90%+ mortality by day 4.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "モルモット子宮蓄膿症は細菌（特にグラム陰性菌）がプロゲステロン準備子宮内膜にコロニー化。細菌エンドトキシン（LPS）が急性炎症カスケード発動：サイトカイン放出（TNF-α、IL-6、IL-8）、補体活性化、プロスタグランジン放出。好中球浸潤で膿瘍形成、組織壊死、化膿性滲出液蓄積。子宮拡張で全身エンドトキシン吸収増加（障壁機能障害）。敗血症ショックへ急速進行：発熱→頻脈（HR>250 bpm）→ショック→DIC→多臓器不全。モルモットはヒト脾臓相当リンパ組織欠落；有効全身免疫応答不可（犬/猫と異なる）。重症化まで時間：閉鎖型<48時間、開放型<72時間。無治療：4日までに死亡率90%以上。",
        "treatment": "EMERGENCY OVARIOHYSTERECTOMY (OVE) = definitive treatment. Surgery delay >48 hours dramatically worsens prognosis (mortality increases to 50-70%). Pre-operative: IV crystalloid fluids (LRS 50-100 mL/kg bolus to restore perfusion), measure blood glucose, ensure urine output (monitor for AKI). Non-narcotic anesthesia protocol (prevents opioid-induced apnea in septic shock): Dexmedetomidine 5-10 μg/kg IM (lower end for shock states to preserve sympathetic tone) + pre-op comfort. Isoflurane MASK INDUCTION PREFERRED (avoids IV complications; guinea pig respiratory reserve already compromised by fever/sepsis). Alfaxalone 5 mg/kg IV slow if mask induction fails (avoid propofol—causes myocardial depression in septic shock; avoid thiopental—too long-acting; avoid ketamine—exacerbates acid-base derangement). Maintenance: isoflurane 1.5-2.5% with IPPV, target EtCO₂ 35-40 mmHg (avoid hypercapnia—increases endotoxin absorption). Local infiltration analgesia: bupivacaine 0.5% 2 mg/kg infiltrated around ovarian pedicles and uterine vessels (reduces inhalant requirement). MAP target >60 mmHg (may require dopamine 5-10 μg/kg/min CRI if hypotensive). Blood transfusion threshold: Hgb <7 g/dL (guinea pigs tolerate lower Hgb than dogs/cats—small body mass). Surgical technique: ligate ovarian vessels (avoid crushing in septic patient—risk of thromboembolism), exteriorize uterine horn caudally (avoid excessive manipulation—risk of rupture/endotoxin spillage), remove ovaries + entire uterine body + affected tissue. Avoid prolonged anesthesia (target <45 minutes total time due to cardiopulmonary compromise). Post-operative: aggressive IV fluids 100+ mL/kg/day × 48-72h (septic third-spacing), broad-spectrum antibiotics (NO β-LACTAMS—fatal GI dysbiosis in guinea pigs), enrofloxacin 10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h × 10-14 days (first-line; fluoroquinolones penetrate uterine tissue well and prevent secondary infection). ALTERNATIVE antibiotic: trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole (TMS) 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14d if fluoroquinolone contraindicated. Vitamin C 100-150 mg/kg/day SC/PO (critical—sepsis depletes stores; guinea pigs cannot synthesize vitamin C). NSAID: meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7 days (oral preferred over SC—better absorption). Gastric protection: ranitidine 2-5 mg/kg PO q8-12h × 7 days (reduce stress ulceration in septic state). Hepatic support: silymarin 20-40 mg/kg/day PO × 14 days (endotoxemia causes liver dysfunction). Monitor post-op: daily CBC (neutrophilia → improvement; neutropenia → poor prognostic sign), blood glucose (>250 mg/dL = hyperglycemic stress response—treat with sliding-scale insulin if >300), lactate (clearance = perfusion recovery), urine output (normal 6-10 mL/kg/day). Medical management ONLY (if OVE refused/not available) for open-type pyometra: <10% success rate; high recurrence (60-80%). Never attempt medical management for closed-type (100% will deteriorate to sepsis within 48h).",
        "treatment_ja": "緊急避妊卵巣子宮摘出（OVE）=根治的治療。手術遅延>48時間で予後悪化（死亡率50-70%増加）。術前：IV結晶質輸液（乳酸リンガー50-100 mL/kg bolus灌流復旧）、血糖測定、尿量確認（AKI監視）。非麻薬性麻酔プロトコル（敗血症ショックで麻薬関連呼吸抑制防止）：デクスメデトミジン5-10 μg/kg IM（ショック状態で低用量で交感神経トーン保持）。吸入誘導マスク推奨（IV合併症回避；モルモット呼吸予備は発熱/敗血症で既に妥協）。アルファキサロン5 mg/kg IV緩徐（プロポフォール禁忌—敗血症ショック心筋抑制；チオペンタール禁忌—作用時間長；ケタミン禁忌—酸塩基異常悪化）。維持：セボフルラン1.5-2.5% + IPPV、EtCO₂ 35-40 mmHg目標（高CO₂ = エンドトキシン吸収増加）。局所浸潤鎮痛：ブピバカイン0.5% 2 mg/kg卵巣動脈周囲/子宮血管に浸潤（吸入薬要求低減）。MAP目標>60 mmHg（低血圧ならドパミン5-10 μg/kg/min CRI要）。輸血閾値：Hgb<7 g/dL。術式：卵巣血管結紮（敗血症で圧迫禁忌—血栓塞栓症リスク）、子宮角尾側外転（過度操作禁忌—破裂/エンドトキシン流出）、卵巣+子宮体全体+患部組織除去。麻酔時間短縮（目標<45分で心肺障害対応）。術後：積極的IV輸液100+ mL/kg/日 × 48-72時間（敗血症third-spacing）、広域抗菌薬（β-ラクタム禁止—モルモットで致死的GI dysbiosis）、エンロフロキサシン10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h × 10-14日（第一選択；フルオロキノロンは子宮組織浸透良好で二次感染予防）。代替抗菌薬：TMS 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14日（フルオロキノロン禁忌時）。ビタミンC 100-150 mg/kg/日 SC/PO（重大—敗血症で枯渇；モルモット合成不可）。NSAID：メロキシカム0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7日（PO優先）。胃保護：ラニチジン2-5 mg/kg PO q8-12h × 7日（敗血症ストレス潰瘍低減）。肝臓支持：シリマリン20-40 mg/kg/日 PO × 14日（エンドトキシム肝機能障害）。術後監視：毎日CBC（好中球増多→改善；好中球減少→不良予後）、血糖（>250 mg/dL=高血糖ストレス応答—>300でインスリンsliding-scale）、乳酸（クリアランス=灌流回復）、尿量（正常6-10 mL/kg/日）。内科管理のみ（OVE拒否/不可能）開放型で：<10%成功率；高再発（60-80%）。閉鎖型で内科管理試行禁止（100%が48時間で敗血症に進行）。",
        "prevention": "Prevention is critical (mortality so high in guinea pigs): 1) Spay all females not intended for breeding by 12 months age (closed-type pyometra can develop even in first luteal cycle). 2) If breeding, limit breeding attempts to 2-3 litters maximum (>3 increases risk dramatically). 3) Mandatory 2-3 month breeding interval minimum between litters; never back-breed (uterus needs time to involute completely). 4) Retire breeding females by 3 years age (risk increases exponentially >3 years). 5) Strict husbandry: clean bedding (aspen/paper-based, NOT cedar/pine), daily spot-cleaning of soiled areas, cage disinfection monthly. 6) Optimize nutrition: vitamin C 100 mg/kg/day non-breeding (150+ mg/kg/day breeding females—immune support critical), timothy hay unlimited (>70% diet), high-quality pellets 60-80g/day. 7) Stress reduction: minimize handling of intact females, avoid overcrowding (≤1 female/5L cage volume), maintain ambient temperature 18-24°C. 8) Early detection: monthly abdominal palpation screening (detect uterine enlargement before pyometra develops), quarterly ultrasound for breeding females >2 years old (detect cystic endometrial hyperplasia/early accumulation). 9) Immediate treatment of any vaginal discharge (even clear mucus = warning sign during luteal phase—may indicate early pyometra developing).",
        "prevention_ja": "子宮蓄膿症予防は重大（モルモット死亡率高い）：1) 12ヶ月齢までに育種意図なし全雌を避妊（閉鎖型子宮蓄膿症は最初黄体期でも発生可）。2) 育種時：2-3産仔の最大育種試行制限（>3でリスク著増）。3) 産仔間2-3ヶ月最小繁殖間隔；back-breed禁止（子宮完全復帰に時間必要）。4) 3歳までに育種終了（>3歳でリスク指数関数増加）。5) 厳密飼育管理：清潔床材（アスペン/紙ベース、スギ/マツ禁止）、汚れた部位毎日spot-clean、ケージ消毒月1回。6) 栄養最適化：ビタミンC 100 mg/kg/日非育種（育種雌150+ mg/kg/日—免疫支持重大）、チモシー干し草無制限（>70%食）、高品質ペレット60-80g/日。7) ストレス低減：避妊されない雌の取扱い最小化、過密防止（≤1雌/5L cage volume）、温度18-24°C維持。8) 早期発見：月1回腹部触診スクリーニング（子宮腫大検出）、>2歳育種雌は四半期超音波（嚢胞性子宮内膜増殖/早期蓄積検出）。9) あらゆる膣分泌物の即座治療（透明粘液さえ=黄体期警告信号—初期子宮蓄膿症発達指示）。",
        "prognosis": "CRITICAL: mortality 80-95% without emergency surgery. With OVE within 48 hours of symptom onset: survival 75-85% (assuming no pre-existing organ failure). OVE within 48-72 hours: survival 50-60% (septic shock complications increase). OVE delayed >72 hours: survival <25% (DIC, multi-organ failure, acute kidney injury irreversible). Medical management ONLY (open-type, refused surgery): <10% cure rate; most deteriorate within 48-96 hours despite antibiotics. Recurrence risk if survived without spay: 70-85% (virtually all surviving females will develop closed-type pyometra within 1-2 years). Females that survive: mandatory spay post-recovery (cannot retry breeding—life expectancy drops 50-60% with future pregnancy). Deaths usually from septic shock, DIC (thrombocytopenia <50K = ominous), acute kidney injury (Cr >3.0 mg/dL = poor prognosis), or cerebral edema. Fertility lost in survivors (even without surgical complications—endometrial damage is permanent).",
        "prognosis_ja": "子宮蓄膿症予後：重大：緊急手術なしで死亡率80-95%。症状発症48時間以内OVEで生存率75-85%（前存臓器不全なし仮定）。48-72時間以内OVEで生存率50-60%（敗血症ショック合併症増加）。>72時間延遅OVEで生存率<25%（DIC、多臓器不全、急性腎障害不可逆）。内科管理のみ（開放型、手術拒否）：<10%治癒率；ほとんどが48-96時間で抗菌薬にもかかわらず悪化。避妊なし生存時再発リスク：70-85%（生存全雌は1-2年で閉鎖型子宮蓄膿症発症）。生存雌：回復後避妊必須（育種再試不可—将来妊娠で寿命50-60%低減）。死亡は通常敗血症ショック、DIC（血小板<50K=不吉）、急性腎障害（Cr>3.0 mg/dL=不良予後）、または脳浮腫。生存者では受胎率喪失（外科合併症なくても—子宮内膜損傷永続的）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Mastitis",
        "name_ja": "乳腺炎",
        "symptoms": {"swollen_mammary_glands", "fever", "pain_on_touch", "lethargy", "appetite_loss", "redness"},
        "description": "Mastitis in nursing guinea pigs is a bacterial infection of the mammary gland causing systemic illness and potential sepsis.",
        "description_ja": "授乳中の雌に多い乳腺の細菌感染症です。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["physical_exam", "culture_sensitivity", "blood_work", "CBC"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Bacterial infection: Staphylococcus spp. (most common), Streptococcus spp., E. coli, Pasteurella spp.; 2) Route: nipple trauma (pup biting, rough bedding, poor cage hygiene), ascending infection from perineum, hematogenous spread; 3) Risk factors: large litter size (>4 pups, intense nursing trauma), poor hygiene (wet/soiled bedding), malnutrition (vitamin C deficiency especially—guinea pigs cannot synthesize vitamin C), concurrent illness (dystocia, pregnancy toxemia), stress.",
        "causes_ja": "モルモットの乳腺炎の原因：細菌感染（Staphylococcus最多、Streptococcus、E. coli、Pasteurella）。感染経路：乳頭損傷（産仔咬傷、粗い床材、不衛生）、会陰部上行感染、菌血症。リスク因子：大産仔数（>4頭、激しい授乳外傷）、不衛生（湿った/汚れた床材）、栄養不良（ビタミンC欠乏特に—モルモットはビタミンC合成不可）、並存疾患（難産、妊娠中毒症）、ストレス。",
        "pathophysiology": "Mastitis develops when bacteria colonize mammary epithelium, triggering acute inflammation. Bacterial toxins cause tissue damage, recruiting neutrophils/macrophages. Glandular swelling, congestion, edema, abscess formation result. Milk stasis may occur from pain/swelling, predisposing to cake-like solidification. Systemic absorption of bacterial endotoxins causes fever, anorexia, lethargy. In guinea pigs, rapid sepsis progression is possible; untreated mastitis can progress to mammary abscess, bacteremia, septicemia within 3-7 days. Infected milk ingested by nursing pups may cause pup enteritis/diarrhea.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "乳腺炎は細菌が乳腺上皮にコロニー化し急性炎症を引き起こす。細菌毒素で組織損傷→好中球/マクロファージ募集。乳腺腫脹、充血、浮腫、膿瘍形成。乳汁停滞が痛み/腫脹で生じ、cake状固化に素因。細菌エンドトキシン全身吸収で発熱、食欲不振、沈鬱。モルモットでは敗血症急速進行可能；未治療乳腺炎は乳腺膿瘍→菌血症→敗血症（3-7日）。感染乳が授乳産仔に摂取→産仔腸炎/下痢。",
        "treatment": "Immediate intervention: 1) Antibiotics empirically (culture pending): Enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg PO q12h OR trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole (TMS) 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days (Note: guinea pigs tolerate fluoroquinolones better than β-lactams; oral amoxicillin/amoxicillin-clavulanate contraindicated—risk of fatal GI dysbiosis). Once culture available, switch to sensitivity-directed antibiotic. 2) Supportive care: SC fluids (LRS 50-100 mL/kg/day if dehydrated), pain management critical—meloxicam 0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7 days (not SC—absorption unreliable in guinea pigs), vitamin C 100 mg/kg/day SC/PO (critical; guinea pig cannot synthesize vitamin C; stress depletes stores). 3) Local management: Warm (not hot) compresses q6-8h for 10-15 min to affected glands (promotes blood flow, comfort). 4) Nursing management: If pups young (<7 days old), consider supplemental syringe-feeding with formula (pups begin eating solid food around day 10); if older, can wean early (day 18-20 vs normal 21-28 days). Monitor pups closely for diarrhea (infected milk concern). 5) Surgery if indicated: Mammary abscess drainage/lancing if abscess palpated; rarely, partial mastectomy if gland is necrotic/irreversibly infected. 6) Monitor for complications: Sepsis (high fever, severe lethargy, shock), secondary infections. Hospitalization recommended for first 48-72h if severely ill.",
        "treatment_ja": "モルモットの乳腺炎：迅速介入：1) 抗菌薬経験的（培養待機）：エンロフロキサシン5-10 mg/kg PO q12h またはTMS 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14日（注：モルモットはフルオロキノロンをβラクタムより耐容；経口アモキシシリン/クラブラン酸禁忌—致死的GI dysbiosisリスク）。培養結果で感受性指向抗菌薬に変更。2) 支持療法：輸液（乳酸リンガー50-100 mL/kg/日 脱水時）、鎮痛管理重要—メロキシカム0.3-0.5 mg/kg PO q24h × 5-7日（SC不可—モルモットで吸収不確実）、ビタミンC 100 mg/kg/日 SC/PO（重大；モルモットはビタミンC合成不可；ストレスで枯渇）。3) 局所管理：温湿布（熱くない）q6-8h × 10-15分患側乳腺（血流促進、快適性）。4) 授乳管理：産仔<7日齢なら補助syringe給餌考慮（産仔は10日齢で固形食開始）；>7日齢なら早期離乳（21-28日→18-20日）。産仔下痢で監視（感染乳懸念）。5) 外科：膿瘍穿刺/ドレナージ（膿瘍触知時）；稀に部分乳腺摘出（壊死/不可逆感染）。6) 合併症監視：敗血症（高熱、重度沈鬱、ショック）、二次感染。重症なら最初48-72時間入院推奨。",
        "prevention": "Prevention: 1) Hygienic breeding: clean, dry bedding (aspen or paper-based, NOT cedar/pine—toxic; replace daily), remove soiled nesting material, sanitize cages regularly. 2) Nutritional support during lactation: ensure high-quality diet, provide extra timothy hay (unlimited), adequate pellets (guinea pig needs 60-80g pellets/day plus hay during lactation), vitamin C supplementation (critical—100 mg/kg/day; lactation increases vitamin C demands). 3) Minimize nipple trauma: avoid rough bedding, ensure pups not too large relative to mother (breed young mothers to smaller males if possible), limit litter size if possible (wean pups by day 21 to reduce nursing intensity). 4) Maternal health: ensure adequate rest between litters (minimum 2-3 week interval), prevent obesity (increases infection risk), regular monitoring during lactation. 5) Early pup removal if mastitis develops: removes nursing stimulus that perpetuates inflammation. 6) Prompt treatment of any maternal illness during pregnancy/lactation (pregnancy toxemia, dystocia, other infections) to prevent immunosuppression.",
        "prevention_ja": "乳腺炎の予防：1) 衛生的育種：清潔な乾燥床材（アスペンまたは紙ベース、スギ/マツは毒性；毎日交換）、汚れた産巣材除去、ケージ定期消毒。2) 授乳期栄養補給：高品質食確保、チモシー干し草提供（無制限）、十分ペレット（授乳中モルモットは60-80g ペレット/日+干し草）、ビタミンC補充（重大—100 mg/kg/日；授乳でビタミンC要求増加）。3) 乳頭外傷最小化：粗い床材回避、産仔が母体に対して大きすぎないこと（可能なら若い母親を小雄と繁殖）、産仔数制限（21日で離乳で授乳強度低減）。4) 母体健康：産仔間十分休止（最小2-3週）、肥満防止（感染リスク増）、授乳期間監視。5) 乳腺炎発症時早期産仔除去：授乳刺激を除去し炎症遷延抑制。6) 妊娠/授乳中の並存疾患迅速治療（妊娠中毒症、難産、他感染）で免疫抑制防止。",
        "prognosis": "Good with early aggressive treatment. Antibiotics started within 24-48h of symptom onset: cure rate 70-85%. Delayed treatment (>3-5 days): mortality 30-40%. Mammary abscess or bacteremia: requires surgery and intensive care; mortality 40-60%. Septicemia: mortality >80%. Surviving females may have permanent mammary damage limiting future lactation. RECOMMENDATION: spay females after weaning to prevent recurrence (recurrence risk 40-50% if attempting rebreed).",
        "prognosis_ja": "乳腺炎の予後：早期積極的治療で良好。症状発症24-48時間以内に抗菌薬開始で治癒率70-85%。遅延治療（>3-5日）で死亡率30-40%。乳腺膿瘍または菌血症：外科と集中治療で死亡率40-60%。敗血症：死亡率>80%。生存メスは永続的乳腺損傷で今後授乳困難。推奨：離乳後避妊で再発防止（再発リスク40-50%）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
